{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Spring JMX lets you create proxies that re-route calls to MBeans that are registered in a local or remote "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MBeanServer"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". These proxies provide you with a standard Java interface, through which you can interact with your MBeans. The following code shows how to configure a proxy for an MBean running in a local "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MBeanServer"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ":"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "<bean id=\"proxy\" class=\"org.springframework.jmx.access.MBeanProxyFactoryBean\">\n\t<property name=\"objectName\" value=\"bean:name=testBean\"/>\n\t<property name=\"proxyInterface\" value=\"org.springframework.jmx.IJmxTestBean\"/>\n</bean>"
          }
        ],
        "language": "xml",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "In the preceding example, you can see that a proxy is created for the MBean registered under the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ObjectName"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " of "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "bean:name=testBean"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". The set of interfaces that the proxy implements is controlled by the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "proxyInterfaces"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " property, and the rules for mapping methods and properties on these interfaces to operations and attributes on the MBean are the same rules used by the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "InterfaceBasedMBeanInfoAssembler"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MBeanProxyFactoryBean"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " can create a proxy to any MBean that is accessible through an "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MBeanServerConnection"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". By default, the local "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MBeanServer"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " is located and used, but you can override this and provide an "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MBeanServerConnection"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " that points to a remote "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MBeanServer"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " to cater for proxies that point to remote MBeans:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "<bean id=\"clientConnector\"\n\t\tclass=\"org.springframework.jmx.support.MBeanServerConnectionFactoryBean\">\n\t<property name=\"serviceUrl\" value=\"service:jmx:rmi://remotehost:9875\"/>\n</bean>\n\n<bean id=\"proxy\" class=\"org.springframework.jmx.access.MBeanProxyFactoryBean\">\n\t<property name=\"objectName\" value=\"bean:name=testBean\"/>\n\t<property name=\"proxyInterface\" value=\"org.springframework.jmx.IJmxTestBean\"/>\n\t<property name=\"server\" ref=\"clientConnector\"/>\n</bean>"
          }
        ],
        "language": "xml",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "In the preceding example, we create an "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MBeanServerConnection"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " that points to a remote machine that uses the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MBeanServerConnectionFactoryBean"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". This "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MBeanServerConnection"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " is then passed to the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MBeanProxyFactoryBean"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " through the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "server"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " property. The proxy that is created forwards all invocations to the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MBeanServer"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " through this "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MBeanServerConnection"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Accessing MBeans through Proxies"
      }
    ]
  }
}
